### Railway

Railway provides a simple deployment experience with built-in database services.

#### 1. Install Railway CLI

```bash
npm install -g @railway/cli
```

#### 2. Login to Railway

```bash
railway login
```

#### 3. Initialize Project

```bash
railway init
```

#### 4. Add PostgreSQL Database

```bash
railway add postgresql
```

{{#if features.redis}}
#### 5. Add Redis (Optional)

```bash
railway add redis
```
{{/if}}

#### 6. Set Environment Variables

```bash
railway variables set NEXTAUTH_SECRET="your-secret"
railway variables set NEXTAUTH_URL="${{{{raw}}}}{{RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN}}{{{{/raw}}}}"
# Add other variables...
```

#### 7. Deploy

```bash
railway up
```

#### 8. Run Migrations

```bash
railway run pnpm db:push
```

**Railway Configuration:**

The `railway.json` file is pre-configured with:
- Health checks
- Auto-restart policies
- Service configuration

---

### Fly.io

Fly.io offers global edge deployment with excellent performance.

#### 1. Install Flyctl

```bash
# macOS
brew install flyctl

# Windows
iwr https://fly.io/install.ps1 -useb | iex

# Linux
curl -L https://fly.io/install.sh | sh
```

#### 2. Login to Fly.io

```bash
flyctl auth login
```

#### 3. Create Fly App

```bash
flyctl launch --no-deploy
```

#### 4. Create PostgreSQL Database

```bash
flyctl postgres create --name {{projectName}}-db
flyctl postgres attach {{projectName}}-db
```

{{#if features.redis}}
#### 5. Create Redis (Optional)

```bash
flyctl redis create --name {{projectName}}-redis
```
{{/if}}

#### 6. Set Secrets

```bash
flyctl secrets set NEXTAUTH_SECRET="your-secret"
flyctl secrets set NEXTAUTH_URL="https://{{projectName}}.fly.dev"
{{#if payments.stripe}}
flyctl secrets set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY="sk_live_..."
flyctl secrets set STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET="whsec_..."
{{/if}}
# Add other secrets...
```

#### 7. Deploy

```bash
flyctl deploy
```

#### 8. Scale (Optional)

```bash
# Scale to multiple regions
flyctl scale count 2

# Scale VM size
flyctl scale vm shared-cpu-2x --memory 2048
```

**Fly.io Tips:**

- Use `fly.toml` for configuration
- Set up auto-scaling for production
- Configure health checks (already included)

