### Docker

Deploy using Docker for maximum flexibility and portability.

#### 1. Build Docker Image

```bash
docker build -t {{projectName}}:latest -f docker/Dockerfile .
```

#### 2. Test Locally

```bash
docker-compose up
```

#### 3. Deploy to Container Registry

##### Docker Hub

```bash
docker tag {{projectName}}:latest yourusername/{{projectName}}:latest
docker push yourusername/{{projectName}}:latest
```

##### GitHub Container Registry

```bash
echo $CR_PAT | docker login ghcr.io -u USERNAME --password-stdin
docker tag {{projectName}}:latest ghcr.io/yourusername/{{projectName}}:latest
docker push ghcr.io/yourusername/{{projectName}}:latest
```

#### 4. Run Container

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name {{projectName}} \
  -p 3000:3000 \
  -e DATABASE_URL="your-db-url" \
  -e NEXTAUTH_SECRET="your-secret" \
  # ... other env vars
  {{projectName}}:latest
```

#### Docker Compose Deployment

```bash
# Start all services
docker-compose -f docker-compose.yml up -d

# View logs
docker-compose logs -f

# Stop services
docker-compose down
```

**Docker Features:**

- Multi-stage builds for optimal image size
- Health checks included
- Non-root user for security
- Nginx reverse proxy configured

