### Kubernetes

Deploy to Kubernetes for enterprise-grade orchestration.

#### Prerequisites

- kubectl installed and configured
- Access to a Kubernetes cluster (GKE, EKS, AKS, etc.)
- Container registry for your images

#### 1. Build and Push Image

```bash
docker build -t your-registry/{{projectName}}:v1 .
docker push your-registry/{{projectName}}:v1
```

#### 2. Create Secrets

```bash
# Copy the example secrets file
cp k8s/secrets.example.yaml k8s/secrets.yaml

# Edit with your actual values (DO NOT commit this file)
nano k8s/secrets.yaml

# Apply secrets
kubectl create namespace {{projectName}}
kubectl apply -f k8s/secrets.yaml -n {{projectName}}
```

#### 3. Update Deployment

Edit `k8s/deployment.yaml` and update:

- Image name: `image: your-registry/{{projectName}}:v1`
- Domain name in `k8s/ingress.yaml`

#### 4. Deploy to Kubernetes

```bash
# Apply all configurations
kubectl apply -f k8s/ -n {{projectName}}

# Check deployment status
kubectl get pods -n {{projectName}}
kubectl get services -n {{projectName}}
kubectl get ingress -n {{projectName}}
```

#### 5. Run Migrations

```bash
kubectl run migration --rm -it \
  --image=your-registry/{{projectName}}:v1 \
  --env="DATABASE_URL=..." \
  --restart=Never \
  --namespace={{projectName}} \
  -- pnpm db:push
```

#### 6. Set up Ingress SSL

Install cert-manager for automatic SSL:

```bash
kubectl apply -f https://github.com/cert-manager/cert-manager/releases/download/v1.13.0/cert-manager.yaml

# Create ClusterIssuer
kubectl apply -f - <<EOF
apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1
kind: ClusterIssuer
metadata:
  name: letsencrypt-prod
spec:
  acme:
    server: https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
    email: your-email@example.com
    privateKeySecretRef:
      name: letsencrypt-prod
    solvers:
    - http01:
        ingress:
          class: nginx
EOF
```

**Kubernetes Features:**

- Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (3-10 replicas)
- Pod Disruption Budgets
- Network Policies
- Resource limits and requests
- Liveness and readiness probes
- Rolling updates with zero downtime

