## Security Checklist

Before going to production:

- [ ] All secrets properly set and secured
- [ ] HTTPS enabled and enforced
- [ ] Security headers configured
- [ ] CORS properly configured
- [ ] Rate limiting enabled
- [ ] Database backups automated
- [ ] Monitoring and alerting set up
- [ ] OAuth redirect URIs updated
- [ ] Webhook secrets rotated
- [ ] Environment variables not committed to Git
- [ ] Dependencies updated and audited
- [ ] Error tracking configured
- [ ] API routes protected with authentication
- [ ] Input validation on all forms
- [ ] SQL injection protection verified
- [ ] XSS protection enabled

---

## Performance Optimization

- [ ] Enable caching (Redis recommended)
- [ ] Optimize images (use Next.js Image component)
- [ ] Enable compression
- [ ] Minimize JavaScript bundle size
- [ ] Use ISR or SSG where possible
- [ ] Configure CDN (automatic with Vercel)
- [ ] Database query optimization
- [ ] Connection pooling enabled
- [ ] Lazy load components
- [ ] Implement pagination for large lists

---

## Scaling Considerations

As your application grows:

1. **Horizontal Scaling**: Add more instances
   - Vercel: Automatic with Pro plan
   - Kubernetes: Adjust HPA settings
   - Docker: Use container orchestration

2. **Database Scaling**:
   - Connection pooling
   - Read replicas
   - Caching layer

3. **Caching Strategy**:
   - Redis for session storage
   - CDN for static assets
   - API response caching

4. **Background Jobs**:
   - Use queue system (BullMQ, pg-boss)
   - Separate worker processes
   - Cron jobs for scheduled tasks

